WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:01.770
- So the Bannon and Manafort pardons

00:00:01.770 --> 00:00:03.800
might not actually shield those criminals.

00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:04.760
Here's why.

00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:07.470
Manafort convicted on
eight counts in Virginia

00:00:07.470 --> 00:00:09.100
and two counts in D.C.,

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:11.470
but jury hung on 10 different counts

00:00:11.470 --> 00:00:13.340
and a prosecutor rarely charges

00:00:13.340 --> 00:00:15.110
all of the possible crimes they can.

00:00:15.110 --> 00:00:16.350
It would confuse the jury,

00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:18.070
but the thing is the Manafort pardon

00:00:18.070 --> 00:00:20.800
only pardons the actual crimes
that he was convicted of.

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:22.490
So that means that a future prosecutor

00:00:22.490 --> 00:00:24.830
might just simply charge
the crimes that they weren't

00:00:24.830 --> 00:00:26.920
able to get a conviction
of in the first place

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:28.350
and the same goes for Bannon.

00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:30.010
Steve Bannon's pardon only goes

00:00:30.010 --> 00:00:31.980
towards offenses, actually charged

00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:34.410
and there's a whole bunch of
other fraud related charges

00:00:34.410 --> 00:00:35.670
that the government could have brought,

00:00:35.670 --> 00:00:37.090
but hadn't at the time yet

00:00:37.090 --> 00:00:38.500
and the same goes for Roger Stone,

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:40.410
George Papadopoulos, Alex van der Zwaan

00:00:40.410 --> 00:00:42.100
and a whole bunch of the other fraudsters

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:43.430
that president Trump pardoned.

00:00:43.430 --> 00:00:46.010
So if the Biden administration
has an appetite,

00:00:46.010 --> 00:00:48.000
they can go after almost
all of these people

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:49.600
and get almost the same convictions

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:51.160
just on slightly different crimes

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:53.110
and heck a bunch of them
actually already pled guilty.

00:00:53.110 --> 00:00:54.891
So it shouldn't even be that
complicated, but stay tuned

00:00:54.891 --> 00:00:57.993
and as always, I'll see you in court.

